## Fall back to live graph when search-cache probes fail

Context: After the Search cache switch, Explorer Preview (and Graph Chat /
MCP find) called ``table_exists`` before querying companions. A probe error
— including serverless warehouses rejecting Thrift — was wrapped as
``Error querying graph`` with no SPO fallback. Search then failed even when
the live triple relation was readable.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py`
   ``auto`` mode treats a failed companion existence probe as not-ready and
   falls back to live SPO (Lakebase and Lakehouse). ``force_on`` still raises.
2. `src/back/core/databricks/SQLWarehouse.py`
   On "not supported for Thrift", reconnect with native Kernel SEA and pin
   ``use_kernel`` on the auth object.
3. `tests/units/graphdb/test_graphdb_adjacency_contract.py`
   Preview and BFS fallback contracts for both postgres (Lakebase) and spark
   (Lakehouse) flavors.
4. `tests/units/dtwin/test_filter_preview_entity_search.py`
   Explorer ``filter_preview`` and Chat/MCP ``find_triples_bfs`` must not
   surface probe errors as "Error querying graph".
5. `tests/units/core/test_sql_warehouse.py`
   Thrift rejection reconnects with ``use_kernel=True``.

